entry.summary:
I added a sort direction to a product search endpoint last week, and when I went to type the parameter I realized the handler already had five in front of it. Search, category, sort field, page, page size, and now a descending flag. The signature had become one of those declarations that wraps onto three lines and makes you scroll sideways to find the closing brace. Nobody decided it should look like that. It grew one feature at a time, the way these things do.
Here's roughly where it landed:
app.MapGet("/products/manual", (
    string? search,
    string? category,
    string sortBy,
    bool descending,
    int page,
    int pageSize,
    ProductCatalog catalog) =>
{
    var result = catalog.Query(search, category, sortBy, descending, page, pageSize);
    return Results.Ok(result);
});

